data=[
 ('Q234','Failed browsing-memory flush removes unsaved events before persistence succeeds','browsing/mod.rs:BrowsingMemory::flush','browsing_failure_probe_receipt.json',
  'The actual public API loses an open segment when a synthetic backend rejects its first write. The error propagates, the store remains empty, but recent_corridor is empty and a later successful flush returns no ids. A successful-flush control retains the same event in memory and on reopen.',
  'Keep pending events owned by BrowsingMemory until save_trace succeeds; commit the in-memory transition after durable success. A partial content-addressed blob write may be orphaned, but must not consume the sole pending event copy.'),
 ('Q235','Failed forget drops unrelated loaded traces while the stored history survives','browsing/mod.rs:BrowsingMemory::forget_url','browsing_failure_probe_receipt.json',
  'With three persisted traces and deletion refused for the middle target, forget_url returns the backend error but mem::take has emptied the entire loaded corpus, including the unrelated earlier/later traces. The store is unchanged. After allowing deletion, retry reports Ok(0), while reopening still yields all three traces. The ordinary forget control removes only its target and keeps the other two.',
  'Remove a loaded trace only after its required deletion succeeds, and preserve the unprocessed and unrelated rows on failure. Make partial-progress and retry behavior explicit; do not take the whole corpus before fallible awaits without restoring it.'),
 ('Q236','Chronological browsing reads concatenate owner segments and can select the wrong recent events','browsing/mod.rs:all_events/recent_corridor/nodes_visited_in_window','browsing_failure_probe_receipt.json',
  'Two open owners named a and z with times20 and10 yield corridor[20,10] and recent(1)=[10]. Two individually sorted adopted traces [10,30] and[20] yield [20,10,30], so recent(2) selects[10,30] instead of[20,30]. The window read likewise follows owner-name order. Sorting traces by ended_at_ms does not sort their overlapping events.',
  'Use one chronological event view for both recent and window reads, with a documented stable tie rule. Preserve owner and trace/event identity; do not infer navigation parentage from chronological adjacency.'),
 ('Q237','Current page-text reads accept corrupted blob bytes that exact-version reads reject','browsing/text.rs:text_of/text_for/load_all versus text_at','browsing_failure_probe_receipt.json',
  'After a synthetic MemoryBackend blob is deliberately overwritten with different valid UTF-8 under its original hash key, text_for and load_all return those different bytes as successful text. text_at on the same PageTextRef rejects a hash mismatch. The uncorrupted control agrees. The current read path bypasses the explicit digest check already implemented in the exact-version reader.',
  'Share verified blob decoding between current and exact-version readers. Keep missing-body and invalid-encoding policy explicit, and refuse a digest mismatch instead of silently using changed bytes for page identity and recall.'),
 ('Q238','A blank Chrome bookmark folder pops the parent path for later siblings','import/parser.rs:collect_chrome_node folder branch','bookmark_parser_probe_receipt.json',
  'An Outer folder contains a whitespace-named child folder and then a sibling bookmark. The blank name is not pushed, but its raw presence triggers pop and removes Outer. The following sibling successfully parses at the root. Nonempty and omitted-name folder controls both preserve the correct sibling parent.',
  'Restore the path to its saved entry depth, or pop only when this folder actually pushed a component. Preserve exact intake source bytes; source preservation does not correct an erroneous projected hierarchy.'),
 ('Q239','An extreme accepted bookmark timestamp panics in the Result-returning debug parser','import/parser.rs:parse_chrome_timestamp/chrome_time_to_unix_secs','bookmark_parser_probe_receipt.json',
  'The public parser accepts i64::MIN as a numeric date_added, then unchecked subtraction of the Chrome epoch offset overflows and panics in the retained debug Cargo-built code. catch_unwind observes it; the ordinary epoch-offset control produces Unix zero. A release build was not run, so a release panic is not asserted.',
  'Use checked conversion arithmetic and represent an invalid or unrepresentable timestamp as a typed parse refusal or absent optional timestamp under the parser policy. Do not let a syntactically parseable integer bypass arithmetic range handling.'),
]
