rows=[
 ('Sealing policy versus retention admission','The low-level optional sealer deliberately allows legacy/keyless cleartext; retention explicitly refuses private keyless copies.',['seal_payload_for_store','retention::retain'],'One shared PayloadSealer seam serves both. These are named host-policy boundaries, not evidence that every LocalOnly cache/write is encrypted.'),
 ('Custody evidence','Retained-copy success verifies bytes and uses a real atomic read/write quota transaction.',['retention::verify/read/retain','CustodyStore','Backend::transact'],'Receipt, body and local manifest share an owner namespace. Nontransactional stores refuse. The source tests exercise AEAD, integrity, quotas and disk reopen; those original tests were read, not rerun here.'),
 ('Seal namespaces and identity','Owner-retained payloads use owner-specific keys rather than the general content-hash blob key.',['retained/<owner>/body/<hash>','seal marker','RetainedCopy stored_hash'],'This actually isolates owner copies. General content-key/metadata alias findings are separate and cannot be transferred to this namespace without a consumer counterexample.'),
 ('Facet validation adoption','The synchronous facet adapter invokes the common schema validator on preloaded definitions.',['SchemaFacetValidator','FacetValidator','validate_payload'],'This is actual reuse, not another grammar. Its unknown-facet Ok is explicit tolerance. Schema persistence does not automatically register or resolve every required class facet at a consumer.'),
 ('Live lineage and durable traces','Browsing lineage reads a Stemma snapshot into per-owner traces.',['project_lineage','BrowsingMemory','BrowsingTrace'],'No second live visited set is introduced. Shared visits appear in each owner view by design; source projection skips nonpage/missing indices and carries no dwell/candidates evidence it does not have.'),
 ('Chronological view authority','Trace end ordering and owner-key ordering are substituted for event-time ordering.',['sort_traces','all_events','recent_corridor','nodes_visited_in_window'],'Q236 proves the advertised chronological reads diverge on valid individually sorted traces. Event-time ordering needs one shared read view.'),
 ('Error ownership transitions','Browsing flush and forget consume authoritative in-memory state before fallible storage calls.',['flush remove(owner)','forget_url mem::take','save_trace/delete_manifest'],'Q234 and Q235 show concrete lost events and memory/store divergence. Successful-path tests alone do not qualify error/retry behavior.'),
 ('Divergent text integrity readers','Current text and exact-version text use the same backend but different verification.',['text_of','text_at','BlobStore::get','resolve_blob'],'Q237 is a demonstrated digest-check gap for valid UTF-8 corruption. Exact-version validation and typed manifest resolution remain separate working boundaries; raw-image integrity remains an earlier candidate.'),
 ('References versus custody','ResourceCaptureStore records caller-supplied retained-content hashes without reading the corresponding body.',['ResourceCaptureRef::validate','record/for_resource','PageTextStore::record_version'],'It validates resource/key identity and distinguishes acquired versus extracted text. A reference is not itself proof that the body is present or verified. Retention owns the stronger custody claim.'),
 ('Projection identity versus historical content','Page-table identity folds each address against its supplied current text snapshot.',['page_table_with','PageTexts::lookup','PageFingerprint::source'],'The content-versus-URL fallback is explicit, and near-collapse is configurable. Trace visits do not carry a content version here, so a current fold does not prove historical bytes for each past visit.'),
 ('Import source and projection','Intake preserves original UTF-8 source while parsers generate a separate typed projection and loss notices.',['IntakeSource','parse_bookmark_file_to_intake','legacy batch parser'],'This is shared parsing with a compatibility wrapper, not two parsers. Q238 shows original evidence can survive while its hierarchy projection is wrong; Q239 is arithmetic refusal, separate from source retention.'),
 ('Transition translation seams','Typed history and raw encounter ingestion have separate transition mappings.',['From<&HistoryTransitionKind> for TraceTransition','browser_transition','history_event'],'Typed history explicitly gives downloads/subframes zero-weight categories; raw mapping recognizes another literal set. Trace the consumer normalization before treating all raw names as equivalent inputs or claiming a current ranking bug.'),
 ('Encounter identity and parentage','Browser encounter ledgers separate admitted Stemma visits from unresolved source-parent references.',['BrowserSourceScope','BrowserEncounterRef','resolve/forget_url'],'Missing/cyclic parents stay pending and owner cursors remain untouched. This is a real common occurrence owner, not inferred chronological parentage. Restored-tree validation still needs a full invariant/consumer trace.'),
 ('History significance versus storage','Hagiograph keeps maximum marks and tied holders while journals own event storage.',['Record::note/merge','Mark::join','Record::reckon'],'The join is implemented by max/equal union; feat uses the prebatch baseline while took deliberately follows sequential mutation. Legends/retelling are described as later work, not implemented by these three modules.'),
 ('Pinned fixture versus live adoption','The Hagiograph serialization test contains mirrored Mesocosm types and pinned expected bytes.',['record_tests.rs matches_mesocosms_pinned_bytes_exactly'],'This is a byte-compatibility fixture in Mere. Reading it does not demonstrate current external consumer adoption, live cross-repo parity or a protocol/trust layer.'),
 ('Deep time uses the supplied simulation','Hagiograph advances Epochal until target closure or a mandatory tick ceiling.',['Epochal','run','DeepTimeError::Stalled'],'This is bounded driving of a product supplier, not another simulation implementation. Supplier blocking and invalid/extreme counters are not qualified by the toy tests.'),
 ('New span proposal authority','Scenomise now owns shared checked proposals, and Graphshell consumes them for copied recipe facts.',['SpanEdit::apply','SpanEditIntent::propose/validate/proposed_facts','Graphshell Pane::accept/edit_copy'],'Source/revision/occurrence/before-span are rechecked. Graphshell assigns the copy revision and validates SceneDocument before accepting. The shared module does not grant source write permission or persist. Source and tests were read on integrated main; no browser gesture or new Cargo gate ran for these commits.'),
]
